//@version=6
indicator("MNQ Reversal Blocks — 60-point session blocks with the daily trend, strict candle-close grading", shorttitle = "RevBlocks",
     overlay = true, max_boxes_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500)

// ============================================================================
// WHAT THIS IS
//   Reversal blocks 60 points deep at session levels, drawn BEFORE price gets
//   there, only with the daily trend behind them, and graded strictly on this
//   chart's own candle closes.
//
//   A BLOCK starts at a level known in advance and extends 60 points beyond it:
//     AS  Asia session high / low, 18:00-03:00   (drawn at 03:00 ET)
//     18:00 open price                           (drawn at 03:00 ET)
//     midnight open price                        (drawn at 03:00 ET)
//     LO  London session high / low, 03:00-09:30 (drawn at 09:30 ET)
//     OR  opening range high / low, 09:30-10:00  (drawn at 10:00 ET)
//     09:30 open price                           (drawn at 10:00 ET)
//     IB  first-hour high / low, 09:30-10:30     (drawn at 10:30 ET)
//     PD / PW  prior day / prior week high and low: OFF by default. They are
//              the levels where a block held least often in ten years of data.
//   The open prices are support while price is above them and resistance
//   while below. A block is drawn only while price is still outside it, and
//   not on top of a live block on the same side. Nothing is ever moved or
//   painted backwards.
//
//   TREND   support blocks are drawn only when yesterday's close is above its
//           50-day average, resistance blocks only when it is below.
//
//   GRADING - STRICT (every candle of this chart, at its close)
//     TOUCH    a candle trades into the block
//     HIT      price reverses 45 points from the extreme it made at the block
//     BROKEN   a candle CLOSES beyond the far side of the block before the
//              hit. Wicks through the block are not a break; a candle that
//              closes beyond the block breaks it whatever its wick did.
//     100+     a block that was hit went on to reverse 100 points, still
//              without any candle closing beyond it
//     OPEN     touched, neither hit nor broken by the end of the next trade day
//   Hit rate = HIT / (HIT + BROKEN). A block is never marked HIT after a
//   candle of this chart has closed beyond it.
//
//   SKIP RULE (off by default)   a block touched while fading the overnight
//   gap, a fast move or a stretched RSI is greyed out and graded separately.
//   With the trend filter on, the skipped blocks hit as often as the rest in
//   the backtest, so the rule is a switch, not a default.
//
// WHAT THE BACKTEST SAYS (README.md, backtest/rb_blocks.py)
//   Real 1-minute Nasdaq-100 data, 60-point blocks, HIT = 45 points, trend
//   filter on. 2.4 blocks drawn a day, 1.7 touched (last 4 years).
//
//                                         hit rate   went on to 100+
//     5-min chart, in sample 2022-24       78.0%        51.2%
//     5-min chart, OUT OF SAMPLE 2024-26   77.9%        54.2%
//     5-min chart, last 4 years            77.9%        52.9%   (1,800 blocks)
//     1-min chart, last 4 years            74.6%        47.8%
//     15-min chart, last 4 years           77.0%        55.4%
//     5-min chart, 10 years                75.9%        53.5%   (5,283 blocks; every
//                                          year 72% to 79%; sizes scaled to price)
//     real MNQ futures, last 50 days       71.3%        48.7%   (5-min, 115 blocks)
//
//   What each change is worth (5-min chart, last 4 years / 10 years):
//     earlier version, with prior-day blocks   76.4% / 75.7%   100+ 52.3% / 52.5%
//     prior-day off, midnight open + IB added  77.6% / 76.4%   100+ 52.0% / 52.7%
//     + trend filter (this script)             77.9% / 75.9%   100+ 52.9% / 53.5%
//     + skip rule                              77.5% / 75.9%   100+ 53.1% / 53.6%
//                    (the skipped blocks themselves: 79.3% / 75.9%)
//
//   READ THIS BEFORE TRADING IT
//   - The hit rate is set by block depth against reversal size. The same
//     blocks on coin-flip copies of the data (every candle's direction
//     scrambled) hit 77.3%.
//   - A 60-point block does NOT give 100-point reversals 70% of the time when
//     closes count: that number is 53%.
//   - It is not a trading edge. Fading the first touch of a block's edge for
//     45 points and exiting on the break close won 61.0% of the time and
//     averaged -2.1 points per block: a loss averages 76 points.
//
//   The scorecard grades every block on this chart's own history.
// ============================================================================

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// INPUTS
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
const string G_BLK = "Blocks"
const string G_FLT = "Filters"
const string G_LVL = "Levels"
const string G_UI  = "Display"

blockPts = input.float(60.0, "Block depth, points", minval = 10.0, maxval = 60.0, step = 5.0, group = G_BLK)
hitPts   = input.float(45.0, "HIT = a reversal of at least this many points", minval = 5.0, step = 5.0, group = G_BLK,
     tooltip = "Backtested at 45 with 60-point blocks. A larger reversal lowers the hit rate: the scorecard shows the rate for several sizes.")
bigPts   = input.float(100.0, "Also mark when the reversal reaches this many points", minval = 10.0, step = 5.0, group = G_BLK)

trendOnly = input.bool(true, "Draw a block only with the daily trend behind it", group = G_FLT,
     tooltip = "Support blocks when yesterday's close is above its 50-day average, resistance blocks when it is below. Backtest: the same 45-point hit rate, about 1 point more blocks reaching 100+, half as many blocks.")
useSkips  = input.bool(false, "Skip blocks touched while fading the overnight gap, a fast move or a stretched RSI", group = G_FLT,
     tooltip = "Off by default: with the trend filter on, skipped blocks hit as often as the rest in the backtest (79.3% against 77.5% over 4 years, 75.9% against 75.9% over 10). Skipped blocks are greyed out and graded separately in the scorecard.")

useAS = input.bool(true, "AS: Asia session high / low (18:00-03:00 ET)", group = G_LVL)
useGO = input.bool(true, "18:00 open price (drawn at 03:00 ET)", group = G_LVL)
useMO = input.bool(true, "Midnight open price (drawn at 03:00 ET)", group = G_LVL)
useLO = input.bool(true, "LO: London session high / low (03:00-09:30 ET)", group = G_LVL)
useOR = input.bool(true, "OR: opening range high / low (09:30-10:00 ET)", group = G_LVL)
useRO = input.bool(true, "09:30 open price (drawn at 10:00 ET)", group = G_LVL)
useIB = input.bool(true, "IB: first-hour high / low (09:30-10:30 ET)", group = G_LVL)
usePD = input.bool(false, "PD: prior day high / low (held least often in testing)", group = G_LVL)
usePW = input.bool(false, "PW: prior week high / low (held least often in testing)", group = G_LVL)

showDash  = input.bool(true, "Scorecard", group = G_UI)
showTags  = input.bool(true, "Label HIT / BROKEN / 100+ / SKIP", group = G_UI)
topColor  = input.color(#EF5350, "Resistance block", group = G_UI)
botColor  = input.color(#26A69A, "Support block", group = G_UI)
deadColor = input.color(#787B86, "Broken / expired / skipped block", group = G_UI)

if not timeframe.isintraday
    runtime.error("Reversal Blocks grades intraday candles: use a 1 to 60 minute chart.")

float bigUse = math.max(bigPts, hitPts)

// The three skip conditions (fixed: these are the values that were tested).
const float GAP_ADR    = 0.3     // overnight gap, in average daily ranges
const float FAST_SIGMA = 2.0     // move over the last hour, in (average 5-minute range x sqrt(12))
const float RSI_HOT    = 75.0    // RSI(14) of 5-minute closes, into the block

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// COMPLETED HIGHER-TIMEFRAME BARS ONLY (never the bar in progress)
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[pdH, pdL, pdC, sma50, adr] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D",
     [high[1], low[1], close[1], ta.sma(close, 50)[1], ta.sma(high - low, 14)[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[pwH, pwL] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "W", [high[1], low[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

// Daily trend: +1 yesterday closed above its 50-day average, -1 below, 0 unknown.
int bias = na(pdC) or na(sma50) or pdC == sma50 ? 0 : pdC > sma50 ? 1 : -1

// What was known before this candle opened, from completed 5-minute candles
// (the chart's own candles on charts above 5 minutes): the move over the last
// hour, the average candle range, and RSI(14).
bool   lowTF  = timeframe.in_seconds() <= 300
string featTF = lowTF ? "5" : timeframe.period
int    hourN  = lowTF ? 12 : math.max(1, math.round(3600.0 / timeframe.in_seconds()))

f_feat() =>
    float mv = close - close[hourN]
    float ar = ta.sma(high - low, 100)
    float rs = ta.rsi(close, 14)
    [mv[1], ar[1], rs[1]]

[fMove, fRange, fRsi] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, featTF, f_feat(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
float spd = fRange > 0 ? fMove / (fRange * math.sqrt(hourN)) : na

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// STATE
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
type Block
    int    side  = 0        // +1 resistance (top), -1 support (bottom)
    float  near  = na       // the level: where price enters the block
    float  far   = na       // a candle close beyond this breaks the block
    int    state = 0        // 0 waiting, 1 touched, 2 hit (still tracked for the larger reversal)
    float  turn  = na       // extreme made at the block so far
    float  best  = 0.0      // largest reversal from that extreme so far
    int    days  = 0        // trade-day changes since the touch
    bool   skip  = false    // skipped at the touch (graded separately)
    string name  = ""
    box    bx    = na

type Tally
    int touched  = 0
    int hit      = 0
    int broken   = 0
    int expired  = 0
    int big      = 0
    int tTop     = 0
    int hTop     = 0
    int bTop     = 0
    int tBot     = 0
    int hBot     = 0
    int bBot     = 0
    int sTouched = 0        // skipped blocks, graded by the same rules
    int sHit     = 0
    int sBroken  = 0
    int drawn    = 0

var array<Block> live  = array.new<Block>()
var array<float> bests = array.new<float>()     // best reversal of every graded block, capped at the larger size
var Tally tl = Tally.new()

var float asH = na
var float asL = na
var float loH = na
var float loL = na
var float orH = na
var float orL = na
var float ibH = na
var float ibL = na
var bool asDone = true
var bool loDone = true
var bool orDone = true
var bool ibDone = true
var float dayOpen = na      // the 18:00 ET open of this trade day
var float midOpen = na      // the first open after midnight ET
var float rthOpen = na      // the 09:30 ET open
var float gapADR  = na      // (09:30 open - yesterday's close) / average daily range, known from 09:30 on
var int dayCount = 0

int  mod    = hour(time, "America/New_York") * 60 + minute(time, "America/New_York")
bool newDay = timeframe.change("D")
bool rth    = mod >= 570 and mod < 1020

// Draw a block at `level` if the trend allows that side, price is still
// outside the block, and no live block on the same side overlaps it.
f_add(float level, int side, string name) =>
    float far = level + side * blockPts
    bool  ok  = not na(level) and side * (open - level) < 0 and not (trendOnly and (bias == 0 or side * bias > 0))
    if ok and live.size() > 0
        for b in live
            if b.side == side and math.min(b.near, b.far) <= math.max(level, far) and math.max(b.near, b.far) >= math.min(level, far)
                ok := false
    if ok
        color col = side > 0 ? topColor : botColor
        box   bx  = box.new(bar_index, math.max(level, far), bar_index + 1, math.min(level, far), border_color = color.new(col, 20),
             border_width = 1, bgcolor = color.new(col, 85), text = name,
             text_size = size.small, text_color = color.new(col, 0), text_halign = text.align_right, text_valign = text.align_center)
        live.push(Block.new(side, level, far, 0, na, 0.0, 0, false, name, bx))
        tl.drawn += 1

// A level that is support while price is above it and resistance while below.
f_addAuto(float level, string name) =>
    if not na(level) and open != level
        f_add(level, open < level ? 1 : -1, name)

// Why a block of this side would be skipped if it were touched on this candle
// ("" = it would not). Uses only what was known before the candle opened.
f_why(int s) =>
    float ex = s > 0 ? fRsi : 100.0 - fRsi
    not useSkips ? "" : not na(gapADR) and s * gapADR > GAP_ADR ? "gap fade" : not na(spd) and s * spd > FAST_SIGMA ? "fast move" :
         not na(ex) and ex >= RSI_HOT ? "RSI stretched" : ""

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 1. NEW TRADE DAY: retire old blocks, draw the prior day / week blocks if enabled
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if newDay
    dayCount += 1
    if live.size() > 0
        for i = live.size() - 1 to 0
            Block b = live.get(i)
            bool waiting = b.state == 0
            if not waiting
                b.days += 1
            bool expire = not waiting and b.days >= 2
            if expire and b.state == 1 and not b.skip
                tl.expired += 1
            if expire and b.state == 2 and not b.skip
                bests.push(math.min(b.best, bigUse))
            if (waiting or expire) and b.state <= 1
                b.bx.set_right(bar_index)
                b.bx.set_border_color(color.new(deadColor, 60))
                b.bx.set_bgcolor(color.new(deadColor, 93))
                b.bx.set_text_color(color.new(deadColor, 40))
            if waiting or expire
                live.remove(i)
    asH := na
    asL := na
    loH := na
    loL := na
    orH := na
    orL := na
    ibH := na
    ibL := na
    asDone := false
    loDone := false
    orDone := false
    ibDone := false
    dayOpen := open
    midOpen := na
    rthOpen := na
    gapADR  := na
    if usePD
        f_add(pdH, 1, "PD high")
        f_add(pdL, -1, "PD low")
    if usePW
        f_add(pwH, 1, "PW high")
        f_add(pwL, -1, "PW low")

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 2. SESSION BLOCKS, each drawn on the first candle after its level is complete
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if mod < 180 and na(midOpen)
    midOpen := open
if mod >= 180 and mod < 1020 and not asDone
    asDone := true
    if useAS
        f_add(asH, 1, "AS high")
        f_add(asL, -1, "AS low")
    if useGO
        f_addAuto(dayOpen, "18:00 open")
    if useMO
        f_addAuto(midOpen, "midnight open")
if rth and not loDone
    loDone := true
    rthOpen := open
    gapADR  := na(pdC) or na(adr) or adr <= 0 ? na : (open - pdC) / adr
    if useLO
        f_add(loH, 1, "LO high")
        f_add(loL, -1, "LO low")
if rth and mod >= 600 and not orDone
    orDone := true
    if useOR
        f_add(orH, 1, "OR high")
        f_add(orL, -1, "OR low")
    if useRO
        f_addAuto(rthOpen, "09:30 open")
if rth and mod >= 630 and not ibDone
    ibDone := true
    if useIB
        f_add(ibH, 1, "IB high")
        f_add(ibL, -1, "IB low")

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 3. GRADE every live block on this candle
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool touchNow = false     // live: price is inside a block that was waiting
bool skipNow  = false     // live: price is inside a block that the skip rule rejects
bool hitNow   = false
bool bigNow   = false
bool brokeNow = false

if live.size() > 0
    for i = live.size() - 1 to 0
        Block  b      = live.get(i)
        int    s      = b.side
        float  ext    = s > 0 ? high : low
        float  opp    = s > 0 ? low : high
        bool   inside = s * (ext - b.near) >= 0
        string why    = b.state == 0 and inside ? f_why(s) : ""
        if b.state == 0 and inside and why == ""
            touchNow := true
        if b.state == 0 and inside and why != ""
            skipNow := true
        if b.state <= 1
            b.bx.set_right(bar_index + 1)
        if barstate.isconfirmed
            bool first = false
            if b.state == 0 and inside
                b.state := 1
                b.turn  := ext
                first   := true
                if why == ""
                    tl.touched += 1
                    tl.tTop += s > 0 ? 1 : 0
                    tl.tBot += s < 0 ? 1 : 0
                if why != ""
                    b.skip := true
                    tl.sTouched += 1
                    b.bx.set_border_color(color.new(deadColor, 40))
                    b.bx.set_bgcolor(color.new(deadColor, 92))
                    b.bx.set_text_color(color.new(deadColor, 20))
                    b.bx.set_text(b.name + " · skip: " + why)
                    if showTags
                        label.new(bar_index, s > 0 ? high : low, "SKIP · " + why,
                             yloc = s > 0 ? yloc.abovebar : yloc.belowbar,
                             style = s > 0 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up,
                             color = color.new(deadColor, 30), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
            if b.state >= 1
                bool  beyond = s * (close - b.far) > 0      // this candle closed beyond the block
                bool  gone   = false
                bool  graded = not b.skip
                color col    = s > 0 ? topColor : botColor
                // strict: a close beyond the block ends it, whatever the wick did
                if beyond and b.state == 1 and graded
                    brokeNow := true
                    tl.broken += 1
                    tl.bTop += s > 0 ? 1 : 0
                    tl.bBot += s < 0 ? 1 : 0
                    b.bx.set_border_color(color.new(deadColor, 30))
                    b.bx.set_bgcolor(color.new(deadColor, 90))
                    b.bx.set_text_color(color.new(deadColor, 20))
                    if showTags
                        label.new(bar_index, s > 0 ? high : low, "BROKEN",
                             yloc = s > 0 ? yloc.abovebar : yloc.belowbar,
                             style = s > 0 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up,
                             color = color.new(deadColor, 20), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
                if beyond and b.state == 1 and not graded
                    tl.sBroken += 1
                if beyond
                    gone := true
                if not beyond
                    float newturn = s * (ext - b.turn) > 0 ? ext : b.turn
                    if not first                            // the extreme was made on an earlier candle
                        b.best := math.max(b.best, s * (b.turn - opp))
                    b.best := math.max(b.best, s * (newturn - close))   // this candle's own extreme, confirmed by its close
                    b.turn := newturn
                    bool nowHit = b.state == 1 and b.best >= hitPts
                    bool nowBig = b.best >= bigUse
                    if nowHit
                        b.state := 2
                    if nowHit and graded
                        hitNow  := true
                        tl.hit  += 1
                        tl.hTop += s > 0 ? 1 : 0
                        tl.hBot += s < 0 ? 1 : 0
                        b.bx.set_border_color(color.new(col, 0))
                        b.bx.set_border_width(2)
                    if nowHit and not graded
                        tl.sHit += 1
                    if nowBig
                        gone := true
                    if nowBig and graded
                        bigNow := true
                        tl.big += 1
                    if showTags and graded and (nowHit or nowBig)
                        string txt = nowHit and nowBig ? "HIT " + str.tostring(bigUse, "#") + "+" :
                             nowHit ? "HIT " + str.tostring(hitPts, "#") : str.tostring(bigUse, "#") + "+"
                        label.new(bar_index, s > 0 ? high : low, txt,
                             yloc = s > 0 ? yloc.abovebar : yloc.belowbar,
                             style = s > 0 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up,
                             color = color.new(col, nowHit ? 10 : 45), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
                if gone and graded
                    bests.push(math.min(b.best, bigUse))
                if gone
                    live.remove(i)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 4. SESSION RANGES, updated after the candle has been graded
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if mod >= 1080 or mod < 180
    asH := na(asH) ? high : math.max(asH, high)
    asL := na(asL) ? low : math.min(asL, low)
if mod >= 180 and mod < 570
    loH := na(loH) ? high : math.max(loH, high)
    loL := na(loL) ? low : math.min(loL, low)
if mod >= 570 and mod < 600
    orH := na(orH) ? high : math.max(orH, high)
    orL := na(orL) ? low : math.min(orL, low)
if mod >= 570 and mod < 630
    ibH := na(ibH) ? high : math.max(ibH, high)
    ibL := na(ibL) ? low : math.min(ibL, low)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// SCORECARD — this chart's own history, graded by the rules above
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
f_cell(table t, int c, int r, string s, color tc, string al) =>
    table.cell(t, c, r, s, text_color = tc, text_halign = al, text_size = size.small)

f_rate(int a, int b) =>
    a + b > 0 ? str.tostring(100.0 * a / (a + b), "#.#") + "%" : "—"

f_row(table t, int r, string name, color nc, int touched, int hits, int broken) =>
    f_cell(t, 0, r, name, nc, text.align_left)
    f_cell(t, 1, r, str.tostring(touched), color.white, text.align_right)
    f_cell(t, 2, r, str.tostring(hits), color.white, text.align_right)
    f_cell(t, 3, r, str.tostring(broken), color.white, text.align_right)
    f_cell(t, 4, r, f_rate(hits, broken), color.white, text.align_right)

if showDash and barstate.islast
    var table dash = table.new(position.top_right, 5, 14, bgcolor = color.new(#101418, 12),
         border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(color.gray, 75), frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(color.gray, 55))
    table.clear(dash, 0, 0, 4, 13)
    color dim    = color.new(color.silver, 0)
    int   graded = tl.hit + tl.broken
    // hit rate for four reversal sizes, from the best reversal of every graded block
    float sizeB = 0.6 * bigUse
    float sizeC = 0.75 * bigUse
    int   nb = bests.size()
    int   nA = 0
    int   nB = 0
    int   nC = 0
    int   nD = 0
    if nb > 0
        for v in bests
            nA += v >= hitPts ? 1 : 0
            nB += v >= sizeB ? 1 : 0
            nC += v >= sizeC ? 1 : 0
            nD += v >= bigUse ? 1 : 0
    float seven = nb >= 10 ? bests.percentile_linear_interpolation(30) : na

    f_cell(dash, 0, 0, "REVERSAL BLOCKS — SCORECARD (this chart's history, strict candle-close grading)", color.white, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 0, 4, 0)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 1, str.tostring(blockPts, "#") + "-pt blocks · HIT = " + str.tostring(hitPts, "#") +
         "-pt reversal before any candle closes beyond", dim, text.align_left)
    f_cell(dash, 1, 1, "touched",  dim, text.align_right)
    f_cell(dash, 2, 1, "hit",      dim, text.align_right)
    f_cell(dash, 3, 1, "broken",   dim, text.align_right)
    f_cell(dash, 4, 1, "hit rate", dim, text.align_right)

    f_row(dash, 2, "All graded blocks",        color.white, tl.touched,  tl.hit,  tl.broken)
    f_row(dash, 3, "Resistance blocks (tops)", topColor,    tl.tTop,     tl.hTop, tl.bTop)
    f_row(dash, 4, "Support blocks (bottoms)", botColor,    tl.tBot,     tl.hBot, tl.bBot)
    f_row(dash, 5, useSkips ? "Skipped at the touch (graded separately)" : "Skip rule is off", dim, tl.sTouched, tl.sHit, tl.sBroken)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 6, "Went on to " + str.tostring(bigUse, "#") + "+ pts before any close beyond: " + str.tostring(tl.big) +
         " of " + str.tostring(graded) + " graded blocks (" + f_rate(tl.big, graded - tl.big) + ")", color.white, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 6, 4, 6)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 7, "Reversal of at least " + str.tostring(hitPts, "#") + " / " + str.tostring(sizeB, "#") + " / " +
         str.tostring(sizeC, "#") + " / " + str.tostring(bigUse, "#") + " pts:  " + f_rate(nA, nb - nA) + " / " +
         f_rate(nB, nb - nB) + " / " + f_rate(nC, nb - nC) + " / " + f_rate(nD, nb - nD), color.white, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 7, 4, 7)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 8, "7 in 10 blocks reversed at least " + (na(seven) ? "—" : str.tostring(seven, "#")) +
         " pts before any close beyond", color.white, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 8, 4, 8)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 9, "Drawn " + str.tostring(tl.drawn) + " blocks in " + str.tostring(dayCount) + " days (" +
         (dayCount > 0 ? str.tostring(1.0 * tl.drawn / dayCount, "#.#") : "—") + " a day) · " + str.tostring(live.size()) +
         " live now · " + str.tostring(tl.expired) + " touched but still open after two days", dim, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 9, 4, 9)

    string trendTxt = bias == 0 ? "DAILY TREND unknown (not enough daily history)" :
         "DAILY TREND " + (bias > 0 ? "UP" : "DOWN") + ": yesterday's close " + str.tostring(pdC, format.mintick) +
         (bias > 0 ? " is above" : " is below") + " its 50-day average " + str.tostring(sma50, format.mintick)
    string sideTxt = not trendOnly ? " · trend filter off: both sides drawn" : bias > 0 ? " · support blocks only" :
         bias < 0 ? " · resistance blocks only" : " · no blocks drawn"
    f_cell(dash, 0, 10, trendTxt + sideTxt, bias > 0 ? botColor : bias < 0 ? topColor : dim, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 10, 4, 10)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 11, "Backtest, 5-min chart, with the daily trend: 77.9% hit over 4 years (78.0% in sample, 77.9% out of sample), 75.9% over 10 years.",
         dim, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 11, 4, 11)
    f_cell(dash, 0, 12, "1-min chart 74.6%. Real MNQ futures, last 50 days: 71.3%. 53% of graded blocks went on to 100+. Coin-flip data: 77.3%.",
         dim, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 12, 4, 12)
    f_cell(dash, 0, 13, "The hit rate comes from block depth against reversal size, not from prediction. Not a trading edge.",
         color.orange, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 13, 4, 13)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ALERTS
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
alertcondition(touchNow, "Price entered a reversal block", "Reversal Blocks: price is inside a block")
alertcondition(skipNow, "Price entered a block the skip rule rejects", "Reversal Blocks: price is inside a block, but it is fading the gap, a fast move or a stretched RSI")
alertcondition(hitNow, "Block hit", "Reversal Blocks: HIT — the reversal reached the hit size with no candle closing beyond the block")
alertcondition(bigNow, "Block reached the larger reversal", "Reversal Blocks: a block that was hit has reached the larger reversal")
alertcondition(brokeNow, "Block broken", "Reversal Blocks: a candle closed beyond a block before it was hit")
